    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hot water didnt really do much. i think it might be a bigger blockage. how do i actually use a plunger though? i've never done it and don't want to make the mess worse.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Plunging is a surprisingly simple technique, but you need to do it right to be effective. First, block off any other drains in your kitchen, like the dishwasher opening, to ensure all the pressure goes to the sink drain. Then, fill the sink with enough hot water to cover the rubber cup of the plunger. Place the plunger over the drain opening, creating a tight seal, and plunge with quick, forceful up-and-down motions. You should hear a gurgle or see the water start to move as the pressure works to dislodge the blockage.",
